data.content:
## The Problem: Missing `await`

TUnit assertions are **async and must be awaited**. Without `await`, the assertion expression is never evaluated — it becomes a discarded `Task`, and the test passes silently regardless of the actual value.

```csharp
// ❌ Bug: assertion never executes
Assert.That(total).IsEqualTo(42m);

// ✅ Fix: await the assertion
await Assert.That(total).IsEqualTo(42m);
```

## Fixed Test

```csharp
[Test]
public async Task CalculateTotal_TwoItems_ReturnsSum()
{
    var cart = new Cart();
    cart.Add(new Item(price: 10m));
    cart.Add(new Item(price: 32m));

    var total = cart.CalculateTotal();

    await Assert.That(total).IsEqualTo(42m);
}
```

**Tip:** TUnit ships a built-in Roslyn analyzer that warns on unawaited assertions. Make sure `TUnit.Analyzers` is referenced in your project — it will catch this at build time.
